<article class="env-lemma" id="011L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011L">Lemma <span data-tag="011L">12.14.12</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Lemma <a href="/tag/011J" data-tag="011J">12.14.10</a>. Let $\alpha : A^\bullet \to B^\bullet $, $\beta : B^\bullet \to C^\bullet $ be the given morphisms of complexes. Suppose $(s')^ n : C^ n \to B^ n$ and $(\pi ')^ n : B^ n \to A^ n$ is a second choice of splittings. Write $(s')^ n = s^ n + \alpha ^ n \circ h^ n$ and $(\pi ')^ n = \pi ^ n + g^ n \circ \beta ^ n$ for some unique morphisms $h^ n : C^ n \to A^ n$ and $g^ n : C^ n \to A^ n$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$g^ n = - h^ n$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the family of maps $\{ g^ n : C^ n \to A[1]^{n - 1}\} $ is a homotopy between $\delta , \delta ' : C^\bullet \to A[1]^\bullet $, more precisely $(\delta ')^ n = \delta ^ n + g^{n + 1} \circ d_ C^ n + d_{A[1]}^{n - 1} \circ g^ n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As $(s')^ n$ and $(\pi ')^ n$ are splittings we have $(\pi ')^ n \circ (s')^ n = 0$. Hence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 = ( \pi ^ n + g^ n \circ \beta ^ n ) \circ ( s^ n + \alpha ^ n \circ h^ n ) = g^ n \circ \beta ^ n \circ s^ n + \pi ^ n \circ \alpha ^ n \circ h^ n = g^ n + h^ n  \]
</div>
    <p>
       which proves (1). We compute $(\delta ')^ n$ as follows 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  ( \pi ^{n + 1} + g^{n + 1} \circ \beta ^{n + 1} ) \circ d_ B^ n \circ ( s^ n + \alpha ^ n \circ h^ n ) = \delta ^ n + g^{n + 1} \circ d_ C^ n + d_ A^ n \circ h^ n  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $h^ n = -g^ n$ and since $d_{A[1]}^{n - 1} = -d_ A^ n$ we conclude that (2) holds. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>